  "coverage": [
    "Actual packaged native contribution is included automatically for selected workflow storage, deduplicated per store, and absent when no selected owner requires it.",
    "Immutable V1 preserves the five pinned vendor PostgreSQL SQL assets byte for byte, apart from assembly header and source markers; source digests separately verified against resolved vendor JARs.",
    "Real PostgreSQL managed native tables match vendor-native creation for columns, constraints and indexes; version/configuration properties match after both engines start, excluding the mutable ID allocation counter.",
    "An in-flight process survives engine shutdown and idempotent migration, then completes with history after restart using databaseSchemaUpdate=false.",
    "Untracked existing native tables reject the entire migration plan before any platform tables or migration histories are written.",
    "Native V1 executes as one PostgreSQL transactional migration; injected external SQL failure rolls back all native tables, and the same script succeeds after resolving that external condition.",
    "Concurrent installers execute each workflow business/native baseline once; full catalog installation and APP/workflow co-storage include the native contribution.",
    "Actual owned-engine storage tests no longer use a provisioning engine fixture; missing/damaged native schema still fails runtime without automatic repair.",
    "Complete workflow PostgreSQL regression now installs native schema through the unified plan and turns off engine automatic DDL; existing H2 fixtures remain test-only native setup.",
    "Metadata API, event/native migration adapters and original workflow runtimes pass resolved dependency gates excluding the executor/Flyway; neutral installation artifacts exclude Spring, JPA, brokers, native engines and domain implementations.",
    "Original service adapter and workflow regression pass after runtime dependency separation; runtime factory reads the actual loaded engine version without Java constant inlining."
  ],
